[3/5] ABLATIONS
==========================================================================

-- Stage-1 only (isolates pillar N3: temporal modelling) --

-- no per-device baseline (isolates pillar N2: adaptive baselines) --
  full system      : AUC=0.9762  detect=89.2%
  forest only      : AUC=0.9755  detect=90.8%
  Stage 1 w/ base  : AUC=0.8847  detect=15.8%
  Stage 1 forest   : AUC=0.8876  detect=0.0%
  The Stage-1 pair is the honest test of N2: Stage 2 can compensate for a
  weaker Stage 1, so a full-system comparison understates the baseline's role.

-- single-modality (isolates pillar N1: multi-modal fusion) --
  timing    ( 9 features)  AUC=0.9662  detect=77.5%  FP=0.0%
  payload   ( 8 features)  AUC=0.9752  detect=90.8%  FP=1.7%
  protocol  ( 6 features)  AUC=0.9458  detect=77.5%  FP=1.1%
  identity  ( 6 features)  AUC=0.8884  detect=39.2%  FP=0.0%

-- adding back log_time_since_enum (the leaking feature) --
  deployed (27 features) : AUC=0.9762  detect=89.2%
  plus the leak (28)     : AUC=0.9770  detect=90.8%
  delta                  : AUC+0.0008  detect+1.7%
  The feature separates every attack class from benign traffic purely
  because post-onset windows are later in a session. Whatever it adds
  is measuring our onset distribution, not the device's behaviour.

-- identity whitelist (USBGuard-style VID:PID allowlist) --
  attack detection: 0.0%  (expected 0% — attacks present benign descriptors)

